{
 "description": "Gold byte vectors for the hep-review-metadata/1 encoding (hep-review spec v9 section 10.3). Each 'input' is strict JSON text; 'expected_hex' is the UTF-8 encoding written by hand from the rules (sorted ASCII keys, no whitespace, shortest integers, \\b \\t \\n \\f \\r, other U+0000-001F as lowercase \\u00xx, quote and backslash escaped, slash and every other scalar written directly), not produced by the implementation under test. 'reject' vectors must fail ingestion with the given code.",
 "accept": [
  {"name": "control_characters", "input": "\"\\u0000\\u0001\\b\\t\\n\\u000b\\f\\r\\u001f\"", "expected_text": "\"\\u0000\\u0001\\b\\t\\n\\u000b\\f\\r\\u001f\"", "expected_hex": "225c75303030305c75303030315c625c745c6e5c75303030625c665c725c753030316622"},
